      "content": "Without Robespierre's iron will, the Revolution would have dissolved into the petty squabbles of the moderate bourgeoisie. His uncompromising dedication to revolutionary purity provided the necessary, terrifying momentum to push the movement past its initial, timid stages. It was his absolute refusal to compromise with the old order, driven by his own towering moral conviction, that transformed a political debate into a bloody, world-altering historical cataclysm.",
      "source": "target",
